The `cardAccount.countInfo` entry picks between singular and plural word forms (`card` vs `cards`, `custom account` vs `custom accounts`) with a `customAccountsCount === 1` conditional. Since all `src/languages/*.ts` files mirror `en.ts`, this forces English's two-form plural rule onto every locale, which is incorrect for `pl`, `ja`, `zh-hans`, etc. The first parameter is also a positional primitive (`(customAccountsCount: number)`), which the plural-form contract cannot resolve.

Return a `PluralForm` object keyed on `count`:

```ts
countInfo: ({count}: {count: number}) => {
    if (!count) {
        return 'All cards use program accounts';
    }
    return {
        one: `${count} card with custom account`,
        other: `${count} cards with custom accounts`,
    };
},
```

Update the call sites (e.g. in `DualEntryExportPage.tsx`, `DualEntryCardAccountPage.tsx`, and `DualEntryCardProgramAccountPage.tsx`) to pass `{count: ...}` instead of a positional number.

The `cardProgramAccount.countInfo` entry picks between singular and plural word forms (`program` vs `programs`, `custom account` vs `custom accounts`) with a `customAccountsCount === 1` conditional. Because every other `src/languages/*.ts` file mirrors `en.ts`'s shape, this hardcodes English's two-form plural rule onto every locale we ship, which is wrong for languages like `pl` (which needs `few`/`many`) and `ja`/`zh-hans` (which need `other` only). Additionally, the first parameter is a positional primitive (`(customAccountsCount: number)`), which the plural-form contract cannot resolve — callers must pass `{count}`.

Return a `PluralForm` object keyed on `count` so `Localize` can select the correct category per locale via `Intl.PluralRules`:

```ts
countInfo: ({count}: {count: number}) => {
    if (!count) {
        return 'All programs use default account';
    }
    return {
        one: `${count} program with custom account`,
        other: `${count} programs with custom accounts`,
    };
},
```

Update the call sites (e.g. in `DualEntryExportPage.tsx` and `DualEntryCardProgramAccountPage.tsx`) to pass `{count: ...}` instead of a positional number.
